WordPress Hosting Platform V9.4 - firewall guidance

PUBLIC WEB (normally always allowed)
  TCP 80
  TCP 443

ADMIN / CONTROL PLANE
  TCP 22 (or your actual SSH port) - restrict to trusted sources where practical
  TCP 81    Nginx Proxy Manager administration - trusted admin sources only
  TCP 8088  Manager backend - prefer HTTPS reverse proxy / trusted sources only

TEMPORARY PER-SITE MANAGEMENT RANGES
  TCP 21000-21999  SFTP
  TCP 22000-22999  phpMyAdmin

Do NOT permanently allow the SFTP/phpMyAdmin ranges in UFW. V9.4 creates exact,
source-IP-restricted UFW rules only while a technician has an active access session.
The upstream router/cloud firewall may permit the ranges to reach the Ubuntu host,
while UFW remains the on-demand final gate.

Example UFW baseline - REVIEW YOUR SSH PORT BEFORE RUNNING:

  sudo ufw allow OpenSSH
  sudo ufw allow 80/tcp
  sudo ufw allow 443/tcp
  sudo ufw default deny incoming
  sudo ufw default allow outgoing
  sudo ufw enable

If SSH is not on TCP 22, replace OpenSSH with the correct rule before enabling UFW.

The manager intentionally refuses temporary access unless UFW is active and incoming
policy is default-deny/reject.
